{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-79372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ that satisfies $y(1)=e.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-79372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}(\\frac{1+x}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{x+1} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1-\\frac{1}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ y & =\\frac{K{e}^{x}}{x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=e$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =e \\\\ \\frac{K{e}^{1}}{1+1} & =e \\\\ K & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=e$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{x+1}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-79372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "94228d1cf50b4ffe133be171eee2ad6084302ecd52a10d818f64b11428885957"} {"question" "q-79372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-79372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{2{e}^{-x}}{{x}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{x+1}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{4{e}^{-x}}{{x}^{2}+2}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{4{e}^{x}}{x+2}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{e}^{x+1}}{x+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-79372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{x+1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3}=4x$ that satisfies $y(0)=1.$  Assume that $y>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3} & =4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x(2+{y}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral on the left-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution\n\n$$\nu=2+{y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nThen  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{2+{y}^{3}}(3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $y>0.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2} & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3}) & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2} \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}} \\\\ 2+{y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}^{3} & =K{e}^{{0}^{2}}-2 \\\\ 1 & =K-2 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "94228d1cf50b4ffe133be171eee2ad6084302ecd52a10d818f64b11428885957"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=2{e}^{x}-1"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=2{e}^{{x}^{2}}-1"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=3{e}^{x}-2"] ["math" "{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2"] ["math" "{y}^{3}={e}^{{x}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(-1)=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =-\\frac{1}{x}+x+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(-1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{1-(-1)^{2}-C(-1)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{C} & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "94228d1cf50b4ffe133be171eee2ad6084302ecd52a10d818f64b11428885957"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-\\frac{x}{1+x+{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{2+2x-{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{2x+{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-2x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-104059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-347853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2}=0$\nthat satisfies the condition $y(0)=2.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-347853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =2x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{1}{2x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{1}{2(0)+C} \\\\ C & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{2}{4x+1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-347853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "94228d1cf50b4ffe133be171eee2ad6084302ecd52a10d818f64b11428885957"} {"question" "q-347853" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-347853" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{4x+1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-355525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y){y}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)=0$ that satisfies $y(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=0.$ Assume that $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-355525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})+C \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C \\\\ 0 & =0+C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-355525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "94228d1cf50b4ffe133be171eee2ad6084302ecd52a10d818f64b11428885957"} {"question" "q-355525" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"} {"question" "q-355525" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{4}\\cos(4x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "46ae69de03d7b9e0089d8bfd3903fa9d931db1b9ebe36f0cb41835ee62455ee9"}] "usage" {"q-79372" []} "basis" 1193 "retractions" [[17592186101452 :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy} + \\frac{1}{y})\\frac{dy}{dx} = 1$ that satisfies $y(1) = e$."] [17592186101452 :question/worked-solution "Combine the coefficient of $y'$:\n$$\\frac{x+1}{xy}y'=1,\\qquad \\frac{y'}y=\\frac{x}{x+1}=1-\\frac1{x+1}.$$\nNear the initial point $x=1$, integration gives $\\ln|y|=x-\\ln|x+1|+C$, hence $y=Ke^x/(x+1)$. Using $y(1)=e$ yields $e=Ke/2$, so $K=2$ and\n$$y=\\frac{2e^x}{x+1}.$$\nUse the interval $x>0$ containing the initial point; the original equation is undefined at $x=0$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186100309 17592186100310 17592186100311 17592186100312 17592186100313] "immutable_fields" [[17592186100308 :answer-field/correct] [17592186100308 :answer-field/id] [17592186100308 :answer-field/key] [17592186100308 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
